---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import "../../styles/global.css";
---

<Layout
	title="Basic Proportionality Theorem (BPT) | Triangles | Class 10 Mathematics | The Concepts Adda"
	description="Learn the complete proof of Basic Proportionality Theorem (Thales Theorem) and its converse with diagrams for Class 10 NCERT Mathematics."
>
	<main class="lesson-page">
		<div class="lesson-container">
			<a href="/triangles" class="back-link">
				<span class="back-arrow">←</span>
				<span>Back to Triangles</span>
			</a>

			<!-- LESSON HEADER -->
			<section class="lesson-header">
				<div class="lesson-number">02</div>
				<div class="lesson-header-copy">
					<div class="lesson-label">LESSON 02 · CLASS 10 MATHEMATICS (NCERT)</div>
					<h1>Basic Proportionality <span>Theorem (BPT)</span></h1>
					<p>
						Master Thales Theorem: statement, complete geometric proof, and the converse of Basic Proportionality Theorem.
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<!-- CONTENT LAYOUT -->
			<section class="content-layout">
				<article class="lesson-content">

					<!-- 01 · THEOREM STATEMENT -->
					<div class="topic-label">01 · THE THEOREM</div>
					<h2>Theorem 6.1 (Thales Theorem)</h2>
					<p>
						The <strong>Basic Proportionality Theorem (BPT)</strong> states:
					</p>

					<div class="formula-box">
						<strong>If a line is drawn parallel to one side of a triangle to intersect the other two sides in distinct points, the other two sides are divided in the same ratio.</strong>
					</div>

					<!-- SVG Triangle Diagram with Complete Proof Constructions -->
					<div class="example-card">
						<div class="example-header">
							<span class="example-badge">NCERT PROOF DIAGRAM</span>
							<h3>Triangle ABC with DE ∥ BC & Proof Constructions</h3>
						</div>
						<div class="example-solution">
							<div style="margin:15px 0; text-align:center;">
								<svg width="380" height="260" viewBox="0 0 380 260" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" style="background:#f8fafc; border-radius:18px; border:1px solid #cbd5e1; box-shadow:0 6px 20px rgba(0,0,0,0.03);">
									<!-- Legend -->
									<rect x="15" y="15" width="165" height="42" rx="8" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#e2e8f0"/>
									<line x1="25" y1="28" x2="45" y2="28" stroke="#dc2626" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="3,3"/>
									<text x="52" y="32" fill="#475569" font-size="11" font-weight="700">Join BE & CD</text>
									<line x1="25" y1="44" x2="45" y2="44" stroke="#16a34a" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="3,3"/>
									<text x="52" y="48" fill="#475569" font-size="11" font-weight="700">DM ⊥ AC, EN ⊥ AB</text>

									<!-- Triangle ABC -->
									<polygon points="190,30 40,220 340,220" stroke="#0f172a" stroke-width="3" fill="#ffffff"/>

									<!-- Construction lines: BE and CD -->
									<line x1="40" y1="220" x2="258" y2="115" stroke="#dc2626" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="4,4"/>
									<line x1="340" y1="220" x2="122" y2="115" stroke="#dc2626" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="4,4"/>

									<!-- Perpendicular lines: DM and EN -->
									<line x1="122" y1="115" x2="215" y2="62" stroke="#16a34a" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="3,3"/>
									<line x1="258" y1="115" x2="165" y2="62" stroke="#16a34a" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="3,3"/>

									<!-- Right angle square symbols for M and N -->
									<path d="M 210,65 L 213,71 L 218,68" stroke="#16a34a" stroke-width="1.5" fill="none"/>
									<path d="M 170,65 L 167,71 L 162,68" stroke="#16a34a" stroke-width="1.5" fill="none"/>

									<!-- Parallel line DE -->
									<line x1="122" y1="115" x2="258" y2="115" stroke="#2563eb" stroke-width="3.5"/>

									<!-- Points (Circles) -->
									<circle cx="190" cy="30" r="4.5" fill="#0f172a"/>
									<circle cx="40" cy="220" r="4.5" fill="#0f172a"/>
									<circle cx="340" cy="220" r="4.5" fill="#0f172a"/>
									<circle cx="122" cy="115" r="4.5" fill="#2563eb"/>
									<circle cx="258" cy="115" r="4.5" fill="#2563eb"/>
									<circle cx="215" cy="62" r="3.5" fill="#16a34a"/>
									<circle cx="165" cy="62" r="3.5" fill="#16a34a"/>

									<!-- Labels -->
									<text x="186" y="20" fill="#0f172a" font-size="15" font-weight="900">A</text>
									<text x="22" y="232" fill="#0f172a" font-size="15" font-weight="900">B</text>
									<text x="348" y="232" fill="#0f172a" font-size="15" font-weight="900">C</text>
									<text x="100" y="118" fill="#2563eb" font-size="15" font-weight="900">D</text>
									<text x="268" y="118" fill="#2563eb" font-size="15" font-weight="900">E</text>
									<text x="222" y="58" fill="#16a34a" font-size="13" font-weight="900">M</text>
									<text x="148" y="58" fill="#16a34a" font-size="13" font-weight="900">N</text>
								</svg>
							</div>

							<div class="calc-box">
								Given: DE ∥ BC<br/>
								Construction: Join BE and CD. Draw DM ⊥ AC and EN ⊥ AB.<br/>
								To Prove: <strong>AD / DB = AE / EC</strong>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- 02 · STEP BY STEP PROOF -->
					<div class="topic-label second-label">02 · PROOF</div>
					<h2>Proof of BPT</h2>
					<p>
						Using the area of triangles formula <em>Area = 1/2 × Base × Height</em>:
					</p>

					<div class="summary-list">
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>Step 1</span>
							<p>Draw perpendiculars DM ⊥ AC and EN ⊥ AB. Join BE and CD.</p>
						</div>
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>Step 2</span>
							<p>area(△ADE) / area(△BDE) = (1/2 × AD × EN) / (1/2 × DB × EN) = <strong>AD / DB</strong>.</p>
						</div>
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>Step 3</span>
							<p>area(△ADE) / area(△DEC) = (1/2 × AE × DM) / (1/2 × EC × DM) = <strong>AE / EC</strong>.</p>
						</div>
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>Step 4</span>
							<p>Since △BDE and △DEC lie on the same base DE and between same parallels DE ∥ BC, <strong>area(△BDE) = area(△DEC)</strong>.</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<div class="calc-box" style="margin-top:20px; background:#0f172a; color:#38bdf8;">
						Therefore, <strong>AD / DB = AE / EC (Proved)</strong>
					</div>

					<!-- 03 · CONVERSE OF BPT -->
					<div class="topic-label second-label">03 · CONVERSE</div>
					<h2>Converse of Basic Proportionality Theorem (Theorem 6.2)</h2>

					<div class="idea-box">
						<div class="idea-icon">💡</div>
						<div class="idea-content">
							<strong>Theorem Statement</strong>
							<p>
								If a line divides any two sides of a triangle in the same ratio, then the line must be <strong>parallel to the third side</strong>.
								<br/>
								If <strong>AD / DB = AE / EC</strong>, then <strong>DE ∥ BC</strong>.
							</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- 04 · QUICK SUMMARY -->
					<div class="topic-label second-label">04 · QUICK SUMMARY</div>
					<h2>Key Takeaways</h2>

					<div class="summary-list">
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>01</span>
							<p>BPT: DE ∥ BC ⟹ <strong>AD / DB = AE / EC</strong>.</p>
						</div>
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>02</span>
							<p>Corollary: <strong>AD / AB = AE / AC</strong> & <strong>DB / AB = EC / AC</strong>.</p>
						</div>
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>03</span>
							<p>Converse of BPT: AD / DB = AE / EC ⟹ <strong>DE ∥ BC</strong>.</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- LESSON NAVIGATION -->
					<div class="lesson-navigation">
						<a href="/triangles/similar-figures-criteria" class="previous-lesson">
							<span>←</span>
							<div>
								<small>PREVIOUS LESSON</small>
								<strong>Similar Figures & Criteria</strong>
							</div>
						</a>

						<a href="/triangles/applications-and-proofs" class="next-lesson">
							<div>
								<small>NEXT LESSON</small>
								<strong>Applications & Proofs</strong>
							</div>
							<span>→</span>
						</a>
					</div>
				</article>

				<!-- SIDEBAR -->
				<aside class="lesson-sidebar">
					<div class="sidebar-card">
						<div class="sidebar-title">TRIANGLES</div>
						<div class="progress-text">Lesson 02 of 04</div>
						<div class="progress-bar">
